\item \code{"linear"}: intercept and slope, i.e. the best starting curve \eqn{a + b x}.
\item \code{"constant"}: \eqn{\ell = 1}. This is solved in closed form: \eqn{f_j} is the
mean of the observed residuals of column \eqn{j}. \code{nstarts}, \code{maxiter}, \code{tol} and
